##
## Cross-sign anchors for the ESP32 modules' certificate bundle
##
## Roots that Mozilla no longer trusts for TLS but that chains servers send today still
## need. ESP-IDF v5.3's bundle check (esp_crt_verify_callback) looks up only the issuer of
## the topmost certificate a server sends, and tries no other path, so a server that sends an
## intermediate cross-signed by a dropped root fails even when the newer root is in
## cacert.pem. ESP-IDF builds the bundle from this directory: cacert.pem and this file.
##
## `ca_store.py refresh` never adds or removes an anchor: a change here is a reviewed commit,
## with CA_ANCHORS_SHA256 in CA_PINS updated and the modules' IDENT_MINOR bumped. The tests
## (tools/ca_store/test_ca_store.py) fail when an anchor has expired, or when none of the
## recorded chains (tools/ca_store/test_chains.pem) needs it any more, so each one is removed
## as soon as it can be.
##
## Each anchor is retired for good by ESP-IDF 6.x's
## CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_CROSS_SIGNED_VERIFY, which checks a cross-signed chain
## against the newer root instead.
##

## Why: Google Trust Services serves GTS Root R4 cross-signed by this root (sha256
##   76b27b80a58027dc3cf1da68dac17010ed93997d0b603e2fadbe85012493b5a7, not after 2028-01-28).
##   GTS Root R4 itself is in cacert.pem, but the modules only ever look up its issuer.
## Needed by (measured 2026-09-29): www.google.com, commodore.net, www.lemon64.com,
##   api.openai.com, api.anthropic.com, www.cloudflare.com, discord.com, pastebin.com,
##   icanhazip.com, api.ipify.org, 1541u-documentation.readthedocs.io
## Not after: 2028-01-28 12:00:00 UTC
## Mozilla: CKA_TRUST_SERVER_AUTH CKT_NSS_MUST_VERIFY_TRUST (certdata.txt at
##   mozilla-firefox/firefox@f6dd0159931e536991eaaa02d839bdffb92c3f22)
## Retired by: ESP-IDF 6.x with CONFIG_MBEDTLS_CERTIFICATE_BUNDLE_CROSS_SIGNED_VERIFY, or
##   the cross-signed GTS Root R4 no longer being served.
## SHA-256: ebd41040e4bb3ec742c9e381d31ef2a41a48b6685c96e7cef3c1df6cd4331c99

